.TH MKPRJ 1 "August 2026" "mkprj 3.0.1"
.SH NAME
mkprj \- create dated project directories from optional templates
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mkprj
[\fB-hnv\fR] [\fB-t \fItemplate\fR] [\fB--var \fIkey=value\fR] \fIproject\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mkprj
creates a project directory named \fBYYYYMMDD project\fR. If \fIproject\fR begins
with a date in \fBYYYY-MM-DD\fR or \fBYYYYMMDD\fR format, that date is used;
otherwise, today's date is used. A path in \fIproject\fR selects the parent
directory in which the project is created.
.PP
The selected Mustache template is rendered to the new project directory. When
no template is selected, the bundled \fBdefault\fR template is used. An
executable \fB.mkprj/setup\fR in a generated template runs
from the project directory after creation.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -h
Show help.
.TP
.B -n
Dry run; print the directory that would be created.
.TP
.BI -t " template"
Use a named template from \fBTEMPLATES_DIR\fR, or a template directory path.
.TP
.BI --var " key=value"
Add a string template variable. This option may be repeated.
.TP
.B -v
Show the command version.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PROJECTS_DIR
Parent directory for projects. Defaults to the current directory.
.TP
.B TEMPLATES_DIR
Compatibility parent directory for named templates. Defaults to
\fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/mkprj/templates\fR or \fB~/.config/mkprj/templates\fR.
.TP
.B MKPRJ_TEMPLATE_DIR
Parent directory for installed templates. Defaults to the bundled templates.
.SH TEMPLATES
Template names resolve from the bundled templates (or \fBMKPRJ_TEMPLATE_DIR\fR),
then \fB.mkprj/templates\fR and \fB.config/mkprj/templates\fR in the current
directory or a parent, then the XDG config directory, then a directory path.
Files ending in \fB.mustache\fR are rendered and written without the suffix.
Paths may contain bracket variables such as \fB[slug]\fR and \fB[client]\fR.
Mustache content may use the same variable names in \fB{{slug}}\fR form.
Templates receive \fBproject_dir\fR, \fBproject_name\fR,
\fBproject_date\fR, \fBprojects_dir\fR, \fBname\fR, \fBdate\fR,
\fByear\fR, and \fBslug\fR. Values passed through \fB--var\fR are also available.
.SH SETUP ENVIRONMENT
The template setup script receives \fBPROJECT_DIR\fR, \fBPROJECT_NAME\fR,
\fBPROJECT_DATE\fR, \fBPROJECTS_DIR\fR, and \fBTEMPLATES_DIR\fR.
